[statement]
A package holding a name, by providing it at a version, excludes every other
package providing it, at no version too: `a` provides `X` at 1 and `b` at no
version, and apk refuses. Contrast `a-provider-at-no-version-shares-the-
name`.

[repository]
P:top
V:1
D:A B

P:a
V:1
p:A=1 X=1

P:b
V:1
p:B=1 X

[request]
top

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
| ERROR: unable to select packages:
|   a-1:
|     conflicts: b-1[X=1]
|     satisfies: top-1[A]
|   b-1:
|     conflicts: a-1[X]
|     satisfies: top-1[B]
refused
